"Contingent Charms": {
  "index": "1",
  "category": "artifice",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Contingent Charms"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Wizards are not much more resilient than anyone else. They are at their most effective when given time to prepare.\n\n"
        },
        {
          "text": "Contingent Charms",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " are trinkets that exist for a number of instances in which a wizard may want a "
        },
        {
          "text": "spell to automatically be cast when a given condition is met",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".\n\nTo make use of a Contingent Charm, first I'll need to craft one. That's easy enough to do at a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Manaweaving Altar",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ".\n\nNext, I'll need to make use of a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Transcription Table",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " to set the spell.\n\nOnce I have a spell set, I just need to hang the charm on my charm bracelet "
        },
        {
          "text": "(equip it in the Charm slot)",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": " - unlike the "
        },
        {
          "text": "Feather Charms",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " these will not work simply by being in my bag. When the condition is met, the charm will trigger, and will consume the spell from the charm."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
